{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373078-what-are-your-mortal-campaign-stories","id":1373078,"title":"What are your mortal campaign stories?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-05T14:49:10-08:00","id":1373078,"title":"What are your mortal campaign stories?","content":"I've heard from a few different people on this forum that Exalted 3E is actually a lot of fun with mortal characters. That sounds cool to me, but I don't really know how to picture it.<br /> <br /> Does anyone want to share, either some specific stories from their mortal campaigns, or some of the general premises of who the characters were, and what they did?<br /> <br /> Or, in a pinch, ideas you think would be cool to do in a mortal campaign?<br /> <br /> Trying to run a game based on this segment from the core book seemed fun to me, but probably not really possible until the Exigents book comes out:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">With the return of the Exigence, heroes come to Great </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Forks from every corner of Creation to vie for the Second </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Breath, while Exigents empowered elsewhere have fol</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">lowed to meet with their own kind. The city\u2019s triumvirate </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">has o</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">ff</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">ered patronage to these heroes, and the services they perform in exchange gives the city new military and economic might\u2014strength it will need to confront the threat of the Deathlord, Mask of Winters. </span> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T15:45:45-08:00","id":1373086,"title":"","content":"I decided to start my first Ex3 campaign as a pure mortals one to ease my group into the system-- the party would exalt at the conclusion of the first arc, so that everyone could get a grip on basic system concepts like stunts and initiative. Even after Exalting, I only dolled out the free starting Charms slowly, to keep things under some semblance of control. At character creation, I had everyone pick a Supernal skill and distribute their Attribute and Ability dots according to normal rules, with two exceptions: Attributes were capped at 4 dots, and your Supernal skill could be bought up to 5 dots. Intimacies and Specialties were normal. They got the full 10 dots of Merits, but I banned overtly magical things like Artifact and instituted an in-game delay on anything that brought in extra NPCs. (I also added a 5-dot Merit to give you access to one Terrestrial circle spell)<br /> <br /> It went pretty well, all things considered. Stunts and Willpower became more important, but characters were stronger than I expected-- on the first night the party beat the crap out of two size 3 battle groups (albeit with poor drill and crappy base soldiers) <i>and</i> an elite trooper commanding them <i>and</i> an E1 Abyssal (with Evasion 4, Soak 8, 12 dice to attack, and a couple low-level Charms pulled from Black Claw and Dreaming Pearl Courtesan). At various other points they persuaded a dead Solar to ally with them, infiltrated a fortress disguised as bird people (and smuggled out a slave), and pulled some pretty well arranged strategic warfare. <br /> <br /> My biggest regret is probably allowing supernatural Merits-- almost everyone took <i>something </i>from the list, which created a rather more mutated party than I really like for Exalted. Otherwise it was a good time-- Ex3 flows a lot smoother when you don't have to constantly stop and factor in charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T16:20:18-08:00","id":1373089,"title":"","content":"AS one of the resident &quot;mortal guys&quot; here, I can safely say that mortals can <i>pretty much</i> do most things Exalted can do, they just have to be smarter about it. You can have kickass combats, moving social scenes, sorcery, politicking, and more.<br /> <br /> I have run several &quot;mortal campaigns&quot;, from the Sengoku Jidai-ish Hundred Kingdoms, where one of my players turned a surprise victory in war into political success, earning a major fiefdom, then gradually using politics and diplomacy to get the rest of the Hundred Kingdoms under their sway, declaring themselves Emperor and planning on invading Vaneha, to not!Post-Roman Arthurian Britain in the North after the withdrawal of the Shogunate.<br /> <br /> It all depends on what you, and your players, want to do. So, in order to answer more fully, I need to know what you want to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T18:01:48-08:00","id":1373111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373078-what-are-your-mortal-campaign-stories?p=1373086#post1373086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I decided to start my first Ex3 campaign as a pure mortals one to ease my group into the system-- the party would exalt at the conclusion of the first arc, so that everyone could get a grip on basic system concepts like stunts and initiative. Even after Exalting, I only dolled out the free starting Charms slowly, to keep things under some semblance of control. At character creation, I had everyone pick a Supernal skill and distribute their Attribute and Ability dots according to normal rules, with two exceptions: Attributes were capped at 4 dots, and your Supernal skill could be bought up to 5 dots. Intimacies and Specialties were normal. They got the full 10 dots of Merits, but I banned overtly magical things like Artifact and instituted an in-game delay on anything that brought in extra NPCs. (I also added a 5-dot Merit to give you access to one Terrestrial circle spell)<br /> <br /> It went pretty well, all things considered. Stunts and Willpower became more important, but characters were stronger than I expected-- on the first night the party beat the crap out of two size 3 battle groups (albeit with poor drill and crappy base soldiers) <i>and</i> an elite trooper commanding them <i>and</i> an E1 Abyssal (with Evasion 4, Soak 8, 12 dice to attack, and a couple low-level Charms pulled from Black Claw and Dreaming Pearl Courtesan). At various other points they persuaded a dead Solar to ally with them, infiltrated a fortress disguised as bird people (and smuggled out a slave), and pulled some pretty well arranged strategic warfare.<br /> <br /> My biggest regret is probably allowing supernatural Merits-- almost everyone took <i>something </i>from the list, which created a rather more mutated party than I really like for Exalted. Otherwise it was a good time-- Ex3 flows a lot smoother when you don't have to constantly stop and factor in charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds awesome!<br /> <br /> What was the premise of that session? Like how did a bunch of mortals get into that situation?<br /> <br /> Maybe it makes sense to just give less merit dots since so many of the merits are problematic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373078-what-are-your-mortal-campaign-stories?p=1373089#post1373089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AS one of the resident &quot;mortal guys&quot; here, I can safely say that mortals can <i>pretty much</i> do most things Exalted can do, they just have to be smarter about it. You can have kickass combats, moving social scenes, sorcery, politicking, and more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for posting! What made you first decide to run a mortal campaign?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have run several &quot;mortal campaigns&quot;, from the Sengoku Jidai-ish Hundred Kingdoms, where one of my players turned a surprise victory in war into political success, earning a major fiefdom, then gradually using politics and diplomacy to get the rest of the Hundred Kingdoms under their sway, declaring themselves Emperor and planning on invading Vaneha, </div> </div> </div>Cool - that sounds fun (although probably a little too difficult-to-run for me).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> to not!Post-Roman Arthurian Britain in the North after the withdrawal of the Shogunate. </div> </div> </div>So this was set well in the past of the main setting? Was there a Great Contagion and Balorian Jihad and stuff? And what did the players actually do?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It all depends on what you, and your players, want to do. So, in order to answer more fully, I need to know what you want to know. </div> </div> </div>I don't have players yet - I'm currently in a Solars game and we haven't talked at all about what we're going to do next - I'm just exploring the concept. So feel free to ignore this if you'd prefer to give actionable advice - I can come back and ask you more specific question after discussing with my group.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T18:17:11-08:00","id":1373117,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373078-what-are-your-mortal-campaign-stories?p=1373111#post1373111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for posting! What made you first decide to run a mortal campaign?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> We tried an Exalted campaign and <i>hated</i> it. Everything took too long, everything was ubercomplicated. We started again, figuring we werent understanding how the 3E rules meshed and this time playing mortals to make sure everyone understood the rules. It was <i><b>great</b></i>. Everything flowed more smoothly, characters were easier to make and more on par with each other, and on my (the ST) end, everything was easier to balance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373078-what-are-your-mortal-campaign-stories?p=1373111#post1373111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Cool - that sounds fun (although probably a little too difficult-to-run for me).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just like with Exalted campaigns, you work up to it. In that Hundred Kingdoms campaign, the players started as Oathsworn, the cultural equivalents of knights/samurai.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373078-what-are-your-mortal-campaign-stories?p=1373111#post1373111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't have players yet - I'm currently in a Solars game and we haven't talked at all about what we're going to do next - I'm just exploring the concept. So feel free to ignore this if you'd prefer to give actionable advice - I can come back and ask you more specific question after discussing with my group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if you are planning on running an Exalted campaign, I, and even the book if you squint, recommend you start out as mortals, at least for a few sessions. It really lets you hammer out any kinks in the system, and allows you to get the basic rules down before you start turbofucking it with Charms<br /> <br /> In some ways, and from certain viewpoints, Mortals interact with the mechanics a lot more than Exalted do, and I for one think the game is actually better for it. Exalted don't really deal with disease, for example, or bleeding, and can essentially ignore different aspects of the game through Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T18:49:05-08:00","id":1373122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373078-what-are-your-mortal-campaign-stories?p=1373111#post1373111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds awesome!<br /> <br /> What was the premise of that session? Like how did a bunch of mortals get into that situation?</div> </div> </div> </div>The game started with the players hanging out on a turtle so big and old that it had forests and an entire village on its back. Suddenly, in the night, everyone was awakened by an ear-splitting shriek, and rushed outside to find that the turtle had been killed, and dragged everything living on it deep, deep into the Underworld. After some initial panic and confusion, two ships were spotted heading towards the town. So the party, you know, rallied the townsfolk, set traps, prepared defenses, and the fight commenced. After the battle was joined the Abyssal, who'd been disguised as a local priest, popped back up and tried to join the attacking dead-- he'd been the one to kill the turtle-island as part of an attempt to get his mcgruffin back to his Deathlord as fast as possible.<br /> <br /> I expected him to escape under the cover of the battle groups. I was not expecting him to get utterly flattened by a mortal armed with an anvil on a stick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe it makes sense to just give less merit dots since so many of the merits are problematic. </div> </div> </div>In retrospect yeah, that would have made sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T19:25:08-08:00","id":1373130,"title":"","content":"I ran one mortal game that lasted 3-4 sessions. Everyone was a mortal from the Blessed Isle, I think one was an unexalted Dynast. They were sent on a mission to plant the flag of the Realm up north on Frosty Dorito Island and investigate the previous group who'd gone up there to do the same and never returned.<br /> <br /> On their way to the north of the Blessed Isle they were attacked by a small army of bandits, suspiciously large numbers of them, a size 2-3 battlegroup. They'd somehow found out that this dynastic convoy didn't actually have any DBs on it and wanted to loot it, but the 4 PCs sent them all packing.<br /> <br /> Then they sailed northward, and in the misty seas of the north encountered a school of fog-sharks, which terrified the crew and send them below decks while the PCs battled them above, including suplexing one into the forcastle.<br /> <br /> Then once at the north base they investigated the former Realm colony up there and found it predictably abandoned, not even ghosts. Then they inflated an airship procured by a northern Satrapy and flew it further north, on the way finding that house Peleps had reason not to want this excursion to be successful, and sent an exalted assassin. She battled the mortal heroes and was killed unceremoniously. Not before damaging the gas-bag and forcing them to land to make repairs, where they had to deal with the local wildlife.<br /> <br /> At last they reached the northern mountains and found the remains of a lost civilization of inhuman creatures. Through exploration and research their loremaster concluded that this must have been a civilization of sorcerers, one where rather than sorcery being a rare miracle, being without it was vanishingly rare. In disbelief they continued past the first mountains into the incredibly high ones behind, finding the other Realm expedition there. What was left of it anyway.<br /> <br /> They found two people remaining, a sorcerer and his bodyguard, both of whom were a bit crazy in their own right. They said they found a crazed titan sealed away in the time-before the time-before the time-before by this sorcerous civilization, but it was on the cusp of getting out. The only way to stop it was to go further down and repair the runes there. Unfortunately everyone agreed this was insane and just decided to leave, the last scene of the game was the mountain cracking open and a great hand swatting their airship from the sky like a fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T14:07:34-08:00","id":1373256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373078-what-are-your-mortal-campaign-stories?p=1373122#post1373122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game started with the players hanging out on a turtle so big and old that it had forests and an entire village on its back. Suddenly, in the night, everyone was awakened by an ear-splitting shriek, and rushed outside to find that the turtle had been killed, and dragged everything living on it deep, deep into the Underworld. After some initial panic and confusion, two ships were spotted heading towards the town. So the party, you know, rallied the townsfolk, set traps, prepared defenses, and the fight commenced. After the battle was joined the Abyssal, who'd been disguised as a local priest, popped back up and tried to join the attacking dead-- he'd been the one to kill the turtle-island as part of an attempt to get his mcgruffin back to his Deathlord as fast as possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> I expected him to escape under the cover of the battle groups. I was not expecting him to get utterly flattened by a mortal armed with an anvil on a stick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Badass! I always love the village-on-the-back-of-a-giant-turtle trope, and casting the players as ordinary people cast into a dangerous situation that they have to fight to escape by the machinations of more powerful entities makes a lot of sense to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373078-what-are-your-mortal-campaign-stories?p=1373130#post1373130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ran one mortal game that lasted 3-4 sessions. Everyone was a mortal from the Blessed Isle, I think one was an unexalted Dynast. They were sent on a mission to plant the flag of the Realm up north on Frosty Dorito Island and investigate the previous group who'd gone up there to do the same and never returned.<br /> <br /> On their way to the north of the Blessed Isle they were attacked by a small army of bandits, suspiciously large numbers of them, a size 2-3 battlegroup. They'd somehow found out that this dynastic convoy didn't actually have any DBs on it and wanted to loot it, but the 4 PCs sent them all packing.<br /> <br /> Then they sailed northward, and in the misty seas of the north encountered a school of fog-sharks, which terrified the crew and send them below decks while the PCs battled them above, including suplexing one into the forcastle.<br /> <br /> Then once at the north base they investigated the former Realm colony up there and found it predictably abandoned, not even ghosts. Then they inflated an airship procured by a northern Satrapy and flew it further north, on the way finding that house Peleps had reason not to want this excursion to be successful, and sent an exalted assassin. She battled the mortal heroes and was killed unceremoniously. Not before damaging the gas-bag and forcing them to land to make repairs, where they had to deal with the local wildlife.<br /> <br /> At last they reached the northern mountains and found the remains of a lost civilization of inhuman creatures. Through exploration and research their loremaster concluded that this must have been a civilization of sorcerers, one where rather than sorcery being a rare miracle, being without it was vanishingly rare. In disbelief they continued past the first mountains into the incredibly high ones behind, finding the other Realm expedition there. What was left of it anyway.<br /> <br /> They found two people remaining, a sorcerer and his bodyguard, both of whom were a bit crazy in their own right. They said they found a crazed titan sealed away in the time-before the time-before the time-before by this sorcerous civilization, but it was on the cusp of getting out. The only way to stop it was to go further down and repair the runes there. Unfortunately everyone agreed this was insane and just decided to leave, the last scene of the game was the mountain cracking open and a great hand swatting their airship from the sky like a fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome!<br /> <br /> If they hadn't agreed this was insane, would they have had a good chance to stop it?<br /> <br /> Did you follow up with an Exalted game fighting the titan? Because that sounds fun.<br /> <br /> How tough did you build the Exalted assassin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T14:54:24-08:00","id":1373265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373078-what-are-your-mortal-campaign-stories?p=1373256#post1373256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they hadn't agreed this was insane, would they have had a good chance to stop it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, absolutely. I don't like to see my players lose a campaign, or even fail at anything, but I'm also not going to have them just win regardless of their actions either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373078-what-are-your-mortal-campaign-stories?p=1373256#post1373256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you follow up with an Exalted game fighting the titan? Because that sounds fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly no, we moved on to other stuff after that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373078-what-are-your-mortal-campaign-stories?p=1373256#post1373256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How tough did you build the Exalted assassin?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm almost certain I just used one of the DBs from the book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T03:33:45-07:00","id":1379206,"title":"","content":"Played a mortal woman married to a Dragon-Blooded in a short-lived one set during the Shogunate that was used to bridge the two generations of a long running game. That was an experience since Exalted games tend to ignore or mitigate a massive power disparity in relationships, but this one was getting increasingly abusive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T07:02:10-07:00","id":1379249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373078-what-are-your-mortal-campaign-stories?p=1379206#post1379206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Played a mortal woman married to a Dragon-Blooded in a short-lived one set during the Shogunate that was used to bridge the two generations of a long running game. That was an experience since Exalted games tend to ignore or mitigate a massive power disparity in relationships, but this one was getting increasingly abusive.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait, whose decision was it to make the relationship abusive? I have very different interpretations of &quot;That was an experience&quot; depending on if it was yours, the Storyteller's, or another player's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T08:00:32-07:00","id":1379254,"title":"","content":"It was my decision.<br /> <br /> Johor Anirah was someone who was either terrifying or rather pitiable depending on which side of her you were observing. For example, she had a standing agreement with her dressmakers where she could pay extra to beat up a member of their staff and they'd be discreet about it, obviously for anyone in the know these instances coincided with if her wife had recently injured or deliberately humiliated her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T10:20:50-07:00","id":1379490,"title":"","content":"So I'm adding my three cents with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379489-ex3-tales-of-the-lost-ages-campaign-actual-play-and-reflections\">my new Heroic Mortal Campaign</a>. I always like mortals in Exalted, I believe that especially for new players the game is just overwhelming and starting with mortals is almost a must. Normally, back in 2ed, I would start in some remote corner of Creation and get the group through few adventures without bringing in much of the iconic high-power things that are WAAAAYY beyond mortal capabilities and would focus on a smaller scale story that would go expanding together with player's (not characters!) experience and potential exaltations. Now I'm trying to bring that up again in 3ed, we'll see how it works <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}